           src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Patches/WildAnimals_Stillsand.xml. -->
      <li>RM_Vaalok</li>
    </allowedPackAnimals>
    <modExtensions>
      <!-- SOLAR_HEAT_EXPOSURE_1: sun heat kind "lowSun" - the Deep Desert (this def merges deep_desert.md + dune_sea.md): "a low sun in the deep desert, so a shield you stand behind works and overhead shade does not".
           heatOffsetC is an invented first value; the owner-watched sitting tunes it. -->
      <!-- STILLSAND_SUN_FROM_LATITUDE_1 (owner, typed: "The biome takes its sun angle from its latitude ok
           the planet not a region description"). The sun's elevation on every Stillsand map comes from the
           map TILE's arc to the substellar point (0,0), never from a region name. Effects:
           heatKind lowSun is the base; overheadAboveElevationDegrees switches to overhead rules at a high
           sun (ruled by card: the cover that counts follows the sun angle). heatOffsetC is the offset at the
           substellar point, scaled by sin(elevation), floored at 35 in the far ring (owner card
           2026-09-30 18:11 PDT: +55 / about 35). sandGlareExposureFloor 0.35 (owner card 2026-09-30).
           All tuned in live play. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_SunHeatExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.biomes">
        <heatKind>lowSun</heatKind>
        <heatOffsetC>55</heatOffsetC>
        <heatScalesWithElevation>true</heatScalesWithElevation>
        <minScaledHeatOffsetC>35</minScaledHeatOffsetC>
        <overheadAboveElevationDegrees>55</overheadAboveElevationDegrees>
        <sandGlareExposureFloor>0.35</sandGlareExposureFloor>
        <maxElevationDegrees>85</maxElevationDegrees>
        <!-- STILLSAND_GLARE_BLIND_GOGGLES_1: unprotected humanlike eyes in full glare go glare-blind. -->
        <glareBlindHediff>RM_GlareBlind</glareBlindHediff>
        <glareBlindExposureMin>0.6</glareBlindExposureMin>
        <glareBlindSeverityPerDay>4</glareBlindSeverityPerDay>
        <!-- STILLSAND_MIRAGE_CONDITION_1: under a sun at 45 deg or higher the far edge shows water. -->
        <mirageCondition>RM_Mirage</mirageCondition>
        <mirageMinElevationDegrees>45</mirageMinElevationDegrees>
        <mirageMentalState>RM_ChasingWater</mirageMentalState>
        <mirageHeatstrokeMin>0.2</mirageHeatstrokeMin>
        <mirageBreakMtbDays>1.5</mirageBreakMtbDays>
        <mirageFullSunExposureMin>0.6</mirageFullSunExposureMin>
      </li>
      <!-- STILLSAND_SUN_FROM_LATITUDE_1 §1-2: the pinned sky. Ends the day-night cycle. Elevation from the
           tile (same geometry as above), clamp lifted to 85 so near the substellar point shadows shrink to
           almost nothing. Bleached-white sky, black shadow. glow 1 = solar panels at full output. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_PinnedSunExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.biomes">
        <minElevationDegrees>2</minElevationDegrees>
        <maxElevationDegrees>85</maxElevationDegrees>
        <glow>1</glow>
        <skyColor>(1, 0.98, 0.94)</skyColor>
        <shadowColor>(0.08, 0.08, 0.10)</shadowColor>
        <overlayColor>(1, 0.98, 0.95)</overlayColor>
        <saturation>0.85</saturation>
        <lightsourceShineSize>1.2</lightsourceShineSize>
        <lightsourceShineIntensity>1</lightsourceShineIntensity>
        <shadowStrength>1</shadowStrength>
      </li>
      <!-- BIOME_ARRIVAL_LETTERS_ALL_1 (DESIGN_PASS X-6/FV-5): PLACEHOLDER text drafted by an agent from this biome's
           own description, always-true list and shipped mechanics, flagged for the owner's review
           (infrastructure/state/items/BIOME_ARRIVAL_LETTERS_ALL_1.md). RM tier: plain reads, no narrator. Heat line follows heatKind. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_BiomeArrivalLetterExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.biomes">
        <letterLabel>The Stillsand</letterLabel>
        <letterText>The sun here never moves, so nothing tracks it: everything owns a shadow, is buried, or carries its own. Do not spill blood on the sand. Water poured out here makes things bloom. Where the sun sits low a roof does nothing: only a lee shadow helps, a rock or a sun shield to stand behind. Nearer the point under the sun, where it stands high, a roof works again. A parasol barely helps out on the low-sun sand.</letterText>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <!-- SALVAGE_WRECKAGE_EVERYWHERE_1: the wreck field (Wreckage engine). -->
    <extraGenSteps>
      <li>RM_WreckField_Stillsand</li>
    </extraGenSteps>
  </BiomeDef>

